# Code style

## TypeScript

- Strict typing — avoid `any`.
- Use discriminated unions for events and commands (`GameEventType`, `GameCommand`).
- Prefer `interface` for object shapes; `type` for unions and aliases.
- `verbatimModuleSyntax`: use `import type` for type-only imports.
- Immutable updates — spread/clone; never mutate props, Redux state, or replay inputs.

## Naming

| Kind | Convention | Examples |
|------|------------|----------|
| React components | PascalCase file + export | `ScorekeepingPanel.tsx`, `ErrorRecordDialog.tsx` |
| Hooks | camelCase, `use` prefix | `useGameSession.ts` |
| Domain/engine modules | kebab-case or camelCase | `applyEvent.ts`, `game-state-helpers.ts` |
| Types / interfaces | PascalCase | `GameState`, `ErrorCredits`, `SubGameEvent` |
| Functions / variables | camelCase | `applyEvent`, `recordRunnerAdvancedOnError` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE or camelCase | `DEFAULT_STRIKEOUT_FIELDING`, `PITCH_EVENT_TYPES` |
| Test files | `*.test.ts` / `*.test.tsx` colocated with source | `applyEvent.test.ts` |
| Event type strings | SCREAMING_SNAKE | `'RUNNER_ADVANCED'`, `'FIELDING_ERROR'` |

## Imports

- Use `@/` path alias — not deep relative paths across layers.
- Biome organizes imports on save (`biome check --write`).
- Prefer direct MUI imports when practical: `@mui/material/Button` over barrel `@mui/material`.

## Formatting (Biome)

- 2-space indent, line width 100.
- Single quotes, semicolons always.
- Run `npm run lint` before commit; `npm run lint:fix` to auto-fix.

## React

- Functional components only — type as `FC<Props>` (see `react-component-style` rule).
- Property lists sorted per `property-sort` rule (variables → shorter → alpha).
- Session reads: `useAppSelector(selectGameSession)` — not RTK Query hooks for display state.
- Writes: `useGameSession()` command helpers or `dispatch` with `GameCommand`.
- Keep files under **500 LOC** — split when larger.

## Layer boundaries

| Layer | May import from | Must not |
|-------|-----------------|----------|
| `domain/engine/` | `domain/` only | Redux, Dexie, React, MUI |
| `domain/types/` | `domain/types` only | `domain/engine/` (logic belongs in engine) |
| `validation/` | `domain/types` (types only), Zod | `persistence/` entity types, Redux, Dexie |
| `persistence/` | `domain/types` | Redux, `validation/` |
| `application/` | `domain/`, `persistence/` | React components |
| `hooks/` | `store/`, `domain/commands`, `domain/types` | Direct Dexie |
| `components/` | `hooks/`, `domain/types` (types only), MUI | Direct Dexie, `applyEvent` |

`persistence/record-schemas.ts` duplicates the UUID v4 check locally (`z.uuidv4`) instead of importing `@/validation/id-schema` — intentional so persistence stays free of the validation layer.

Domain logic changes belong in `src/domain/engine/` with tests in `*.test.ts` beside the module.
